.TH GOCAT-SNIFFER 1 "December 2024" "GoCat 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
gocat-sniffer \- network packet sniffer
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B gocat sniffer
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Capture and analyze network packets with BPF filtering support.
Requires root/administrator privileges for packet capture.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-i ", " \-\-interface " " \fINAME\fR
Network interface to sniff
.TP
.BR \-f ", " \-\-filter " " \fIEXPRESSION\fR
BPF filter expression
.TP
.BR \-\-promisc
Enable promiscuous mode (default: true)
.TP
.BR \-\-snaplen " " \fILENGTH\fR
Snapshot length (default: 65535)
.TP
.BR \-\-timeout " " \fIDURATION\fR
Read timeout (default: 30s)
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-count " " \fINUM\fR
Number of packets to capture (0=unlimited)
.TP
.BR \-\-sniff\-verbose
Verbose output
.TP
.BR \-\-decode
Decode packet contents
.TP
.BR \-o ", " \-\-output " " \fIFILE\fR
Save packets to pcap file
.SH FILTER EXPRESSIONS
BPF filter expressions can be used to filter packets:
.TP
.B tcp
Capture only TCP packets
.TP
.B udp
Capture only UDP packets
.TP
.B port 80
Capture packets on port 80
.TP
.B host 192.168.1.1
Capture packets to/from host
.TP
.B net 192.168.1.0/24
Capture packets in network
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
List interfaces:
.B sudo gocat sniffer
.TP
Capture on eth0:
.B sudo gocat sniffer -i eth0
.TP
Capture HTTP traffic:
.B sudo gocat sniffer -i eth0 -f "tcp port 80"
.TP
Save to file:
.B sudo gocat sniffer -i eth0 -o capture.pcap
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR gocat (1),
.BR tcpdump (1),
.BR wireshark (1)
